.Dd March 12, 2026
.Dt DEVICE_PM 9
.Os Substrate
.Sh NAME
.Nm device_suspend ,
.Nm device_resume
.Nd suspend and resume a device tree
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In kern/device.h
.Ft int
.Fn device_suspend "struct device *dev" "pm_state_t state"
.Ft int
.Fn device_resume "struct device *dev"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Fn device_suspend
function recursively suspends a device subtree.
Child devices are suspended before their parent so downstream devices quiesce
before shared upstream transport state is powered down.
.Pp
The
.Fn device_resume
function recursively resumes a device subtree.
The parent device is resumed before its children so downstream devices see an
already-restored upstream path.
.Pp
If present, the bound driver's
.Va suspend
and
.Va resume
callbacks are invoked for each device in the required order.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
These functions return 0 on success or a non-zero error from the first failing
driver callback.
Passing a
.Dv NULL
device returns
.Dv -EINVAL .
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr device 9 ,
.Xr driver 9
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
interfaces first appeared in Substrate.
